      "exampleEnglish": "If the man who works in the office goes, he will eat.",
      "grammarNote": "A closing capstone for levels 51-60: the إِذَا conditional (level 57) wrapped around a relative clause (level 55, الرجل الذي يعمل في المكتب, reusing يعمل from level 33 and في المكتب from levels 5/31), with a سَـ-future result clause (level 41) built on يَأْكُلُ ('he eats', level 25) — سَيَأْكُلُ, 'he will eat', the same reuse trick as ever. 60 of 100 levels now authored. دَائِمًا ('always') takes the same accusative -ًا ending you've now seen on غَدًا, جِدًّا, أَيْضًا, and قَلِيلًا — a small, recurring family of adverbs.",
